    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-024-06037-4>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "Individual cells transposed from one anterior-posterior axial domain to another will change their gene expression to match their neighbors159,161,162. In contrast, groups of cells transposed along the anterior-posterior axis maintain their original gene expression, thus resisting the inductive effects of the surrounding tissue159,161,162.".
